sub("**Test seam (readiness major 2).** An injected `llm=` argument to `app.build` skips `make`. Rule, checked at the end of the `app.build` llm step: if any paid kind is configured and `llm` is not a `FakeLLM`, then `getattr(llm, \"gate\", None)` must be a `CallGate`, else `ConfigError(\"llm built without a spend gate\")`. This covers `NetworkLLM` subclasses and any other class (security minor 4). Not covered, and stated: a test that assigns `.llm =` after `build` (`tests/test_p5p6_followups.py:101` and the three other sites of F16) bypasses the check by design. Which of the 38 test hits pass a `NetworkLLM` into `app.build` is **not known**: E0-S1-1 lists them as failures if any exist and the S-1 builder gives them `gate=None`-free fixtures.","**No gate means no paid kind (security major M2: v10 guarded a missing gate only by a source census).** `NetworkLLM.__init__(self, routes, max_attempts, sleep=time.sleep, *, gate, unmetered=False)`: the keyword `gate` has **no default**; `gate=None` is accepted only together with `unmetered=True`; anything else raises `ConfigError(\"a paid model kind needs a spend gate\")`. The `make()` of each of the four kinds passes `gate=deps.gate` and raises that same error when `deps.gate` is `None`; `unmetered` is not in `ALLOWED`, so a configured backend can never be built unmetered. `GuardrailDetector` has the same rule. So the control no longer rests on a census of our own source: a client build, a direct construction and a `make(\"llm\", ...)` call with `deps.gate` unset all fail, and a test that wants a gate-less kind must say `unmetered=True` out loud. Census C5 (S-1) fails if `unmetered=True` appears in `src/` or `demos/`. Tests that build the kinds directly (`tests/test_p5_llm.py`, `tests/test_p1a_fixes.py` and others; the S-1 builder lists them from E0-S1-1) get `unmetered=True`.\n\n**Test seam (readiness major 2 of v9, kept).** An injected `llm=` argument to `app.build` skips `make`. Rule, checked at the end of the `app.build` llm step: if any paid kind is configured and `llm` is not a `FakeLLM`, then `getattr(llm, \"gate\", None)` must be a `CallGate`, else `ConfigError(\"llm built without a spend gate\")`. Not covered, and stated: a test that assigns `.llm =` or `.detector =` after `build` (five sites, F16) bypasses the check by design; a class that is not a `NetworkLLM` (a scripted test model) has no gate by construction and is not a paid kind.")
